Appendix I: Complete Phase Diagram Characterization

I.1 Two-Parameter Phase Diagram ($\lambda$ vs. $A$)

For fixed $(R, \gamma, \tau, b, v, s, \mathcal{K}, \sigma_0, q_0, \theta)$, the cooperative region in $(\lambda, A)$ space is characterized by:

\Theta_C = \{(\lambda, A) : F_1(\lambda, A) \geq 0 \land F_2(\lambda, A) \geq 0\}

where $F_1$ and $F_2$ are the asymmetric cooperation functions.

Phase boundaries:

· Lower boundary: $\lambda = \lambda^*$ (minimum interdependence for cooperation)
· Upper boundary: $A = A^*(\lambda)$ (maximum asymmetry for cooperation)

Regions:

· $\Theta_C$: Cooperation sustainable
· $\Theta \setminus \Theta_C$: Cooperation not sustainable
· Subregion of $\Theta \setminus \Theta_C$ with $A > A^*$: Weaponized interdependence regime

I.2 Two-Parameter Phase Diagram ($\gamma$ vs. $\tau$)

For fixed $(\lambda, A, R, b, v, s, \kappa_0, \eta, \mu, \sigma_0, q_0, \tau_0, \theta)$, the cooperative region in $(\gamma, \tau)$ space:

\Theta_C = \{(\gamma, \tau) : F(\gamma, \tau) \geq 0\}

where:

F(\gamma, \tau) = \lambda b - \alpha + \lambda v(1-s)\kappa_0\gamma^\eta(1+\mu\tau)(1-R)\sigma_0q_0e^{-\tau/\tau_0}\bar{g}

Phase boundary: $F(\gamma, \tau) = 0$

Solving for $\gamma$ as a function of $\tau$:

\gamma^*(\tau) = \left[\frac{\alpha - \lambda b}{\lambda v(1-s)\kappa_0(1+\mu\tau)(1-R)\sigma_0q_0e^{-\tau/\tau_0}\bar{g}}\right]^{1/\eta}

The cooperative region is $\{(\gamma, \tau) : \gamma \leq \gamma^*(\tau)\}$ (in the static model without preemption).

I.3 Three-Parameter Phase Diagram ($\lambda$, $R$, $\tau$)

The cooperative region is a three-dimensional volume bounded by the surface:

\lambda = \frac{\alpha}{b + v(1-s)\mathcal{K}(\gamma,\tau)(1-R)\sigma(\tau)}

This surface has the following properties:

· Monotonically increasing in $R$ (higher redundancy requires higher $\lambda$)
· Non-monotonic in $\tau$ (increases then decreases as delay grows)
· The volume of $\Theta_C$ is finite and depends on parameter ranges

